4:   "summary": "Input task: I inspected the code and made no changes. I did not run anything, because no execution tool is available.\n\nChanged files: none.\n\nDigest: 6ef3e2af1bf51ab5ffc051b67b311a2a3e889da805d322913d19fe02deb9af12.\n\nWhat I read:\n- loop/acceptance.md and platform/README.md.\n- platform/doomgeneric_wasm.c and web/index.html.\n- third_party/doomgeneric/doomkeys.h.\n- Prior handoffs: build-03 reviewer and rendering-01 tester.\n- The build-03 verification result.json.\n- I did not open the other listed prior handoffs, process files or tests.\n\nFindings:\n- **Key codes:** The MAP in web/index.html (lines 30-41) matches doomkeys.h.\n  - Arrows are 0xac/0xad/0xae/0xaf, strafe is 0xa0/0xa1, use is 0xa2, and fire is 0xa3 (Ctrl).\n  - Enter is 13, Esc is 27, Tab is 9, Shift is 0x80+0x36, and Pause/P is 0xff.\n  - Letters are lowercased, and digits 1-7 map to weapons.\n- **Movement and turning:** The arrow keys and W/S/A/D reach `dg_key` through a ring buffer (platform/doomgeneric_wasm.c:67-87), and `DG_GetKey` drains it in order.\n- **Overlapping keys:** The `down` map in `send` and `release` (index.html:48-69) tracks aliases such as ArrowUp and W. A shared Doom key is released only when no physical key still holds it.\n- **Key release:** `keyup` always releases. `blur` and `visibilitychange` call `releaseAll`, which sends release for every held key.\n- **Toolbar buttons:** Menu and Pause tap Esc and Pause via `buttonKey`, which presses, releases after 70 ms, and refocuses the canvas.\n- **Test evidence:** The build-03 tester verification-c2ca2bd026bb ran at this same digest and returned PASS (build rc 0, tests rc 0). The acceptance scope lists movement, turning, ammo consumed by firing, use-key delivery and release, synthetic blur release, alternate keys, weapons, automap and pause/resume as covered by those tests. I took this from the acceptance text and the recorded result, not from reading the tests.\n\nRemaining defects: none found in the automated scope.\n\nGaps, none confirmed as defects:\n- Real OS focus loss is not tested; only a synthetic blur is.\n- Mouse aiming is not implemented, because mouse events are commented out in the engine's i_input.c, which is protected.\n- Actual door and switch activation, a manual playthrough, and the full-capstone items (teammate exercise NOT PERFORMED) are not covered by these checks.\n- A key held while focus sits on a toolbar button is ignored by design.\n\nHuman-owned changes: none required.\n\nEvidence needed: a fresh tester verification at the current digest, and a manual playthrough if full acceptance is wanted. DONE means this was handed off, not accepted.",
