4:   "summary": "PASS for the scoped input task (movement, turning, shooting, key release, browser controls) at digest 6ef3e2af1bf51ab5ffc051b67b311a2a3e889da805d322913d19fe02deb9af12. I found no defects. I could not run code, so I did not run the tests myself.\n\nWhat I read:\n- loop/acceptance.md\n- the input-01 coder handoff\n- web/index.html\n- platform/doomgeneric_wasm.c\n- tests/browser.mjs\n- artifacts/runs/loop-20261105T005309Z-73a58c79/build-03-739c40e3/tester/verification-c2ca2bd026bb/result.json\n- I did not open the other listed prior handoffs, process files or failure records.\n\nFindings:\n- **Coder changes:** the coder made no changes. I treated its claims as unproven and checked the source myself.\n- **Key mapping:** web/index.html:30-47 maps the arrows, W/S/A/D, Ctrl (fire), Space (use), Shift (run), Tab, digits and P/Pause. The coder cited doomkeys.h to confirm the codes, and I did not open that file. The 0xa0\u20130xaf values are consistent with the standard doomgeneric values.\n- **Key queue:** `dg_key` in platform/doomgeneric_wasm.c:81-87 feeds a ring buffer. It ignores a key that is out of range or arrives when the queue is full. `DG_GetKey` drains it in order (lines 67-74).\n- **Key release:** the `down` map (index.html:48-69) tracks physical-key aliases such as ArrowUp and W, or left and right Shift. A shared Doom key is released only when no physical key still holds it. `keyup` always releases, including when focus is on a button. `blur` and `visibilitychange` call `releaseAll` (lines 72-77).\n- **Controls:** the Menu and Pause buttons tap Esc and Pause for 70 ms and then refocus the canvas (lines 79-86). A keydown that lands on a button, input, select or textarea is ignored by design.\n- **Existing checks:** tests/browser.mjs drives real CDP key events (never calls `dg_key` directly) and checks the following:\n  - position change and canvas update after movement\n  - angle change after turning\n  - ammunition consumed by firing\n  - use-key press and release\n  - W/S/A/D movement and strafing\n  - Shift run, including overlapping left and right Shift\n  - weapon selection\n  - automap\n  - Menu and Pause buttons and the P shortcut\n  - release of a held turn key after a synthetic blur\n- **Test record:** the recorded verification result.json shows PASS at this digest, with build return code 0 and tests return code 0. I am relying on that file for the test outcome. I did not inspect the test run's own output.\n\nMinor risks, not defects:\n- A key held while Cmd is pressed on macOS could miss its keyup. The `blur` handler mitigates this.\n- Alt or Tab OS shortcuts rely on `blur` to release keys.\n- A held Pause/Esc button tap is fixed at 70 ms. The engine could miss it at a very low frame rate. The tests did not show this.\n\nNot covered by the automated checks (manual or separate evidence required):\n- real OS focus transitions (only a synthetic blur is tested)\n- mouse aiming (not implemented; mouse events are disabled in the protected engine input code)\n- actual door or switch activation (the use check only reads engine input state)\n- physical audio and musical fidelity\n- save persistence\n- a manual playthrough\n\nThis PASS is not full capstone acceptance. The two-regression autonomous repair, resumption and live-loop evidence, and the reflection are separate requirements. The teammate exercise is NOT PERFORMED, as requested by the user.\n\nEvidence paths:\n- loop/acceptance.md\n- web/index.html\n- platform/doomgeneric_wasm.c\n- tests/browser.mjs\n- artifacts/runs/loop-20261105T005309Z-73a58c79/build-03-739c40e3/tester/verification-c2ca2bd026bb/result.json\n- artifacts/runs/loop-20261105T005309Z-73a58c79/input-01-5aeea48a/coder/handoff.json\n\nA fresh tester verification is still required to tie the final PASS to the source hash.",
